---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A service that can do 100 requests per second normally gets 60. A spike hits at second 10. Clients give up after the timeout. Pick how the server protects itself and watch useful work, not busy work.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default is <b>no protection</b>: an unbounded FIFO queue, a 15 second spike at 3x capacity (300 req/s), a 2 second client timeout. The server stays 100% busy, yet <b>goodput</b> (answers that arrive in time) falls from 60 to about 19 req/s over the spike, about 8,400 requests are served for callers that already left (<b>wasted work</b>), and goodput only returns to normal about 72 seconds <i>after</i> the spike ended, while the old backlog drains.</li>
    <li>Switch <b>Policy</b> to <b>Static limit, fail fast</b> (limit 50): goodput holds at about 80 req/s with 610 ms latency, nothing is wasted, and recovery is immediate. Raise the <b>limit</b> to 400 (queue wait of 4 s, longer than the timeout) and it collapses again to about 18 req/s with 1,663 requests wasted: a bound is only safe below <i>capacity x timeout</i>. Choose <b>Adaptive</b> and the same overload is handled without a hand-picked number (about 81 req/s, 368 ms), settling near a limit of 30.</li>
    <li>With <b>Policy</b> back on <b>Static limit, fail fast</b> (limit 50) and <b>Clients retry</b> set to <b>Retry at once (3 tries)</b> and the static limit, goodput drops to about 61 req/s because every rejection comes back three times and rejecting is not free. Change <b>Cost of a rejection</b> to <b>Edge proxy (1%)</b> and it recovers to about 90; set it to <b>Deep in the app (20%)</b> and goodput collapses to about 2 req/s: shed early, where it is cheap.</li>
    <li>Compare <b>LIFO + drop oldest</b> with the static limit: the same goodput (about 80 req/s) but latency of 100 ms instead of 610 ms, because the newest request, the one whose caller is still waiting, is served first. Try <b>Priority</b>: all critical traffic (one request in five) is served while normal traffic is shed first, but at a 5x spike the critical share alone fills capacity and drops to about 71%, so the critical class needs its own ceiling too. On unbounded FIFO, tick <b>Server skips requests whose caller has gone</b>: goodput jumps to about 100 req/s with no shedding at all, but latency sits at about 1.8 s, near the timeout.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg ls" data-ls>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Policy <select class="pg-in" data-policy>
        <option value="fifo" selected>No protection (unbounded FIFO)</option>
        <option value="bounded">Static limit, fail fast (bounded queue)</option>
        <option value="adaptive">Adaptive limit (AIMD on queue delay)</option>
        <option value="lifo">LIFO + drop oldest</option>
        <option value="priority">Priority shedding</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Clients retry <select class="pg-in" data-retry>
        <option value="none" selected>Never</option>
        <option value="naive">Retry at once (3 tries)</option>
        <option value="backoff">Backoff + jitter (3 tries)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Cost of a rejection <select class="pg-in" data-reject>
        <option value="1">Edge proxy (1%)</option>
        <option value="5" selected>In the app (5%)</option>
        <option value="20">Deep in the app (20%)</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Spike size <input type="range" min="1.5" max="6" step="0.5" value="3" data-mult /> <b data-multval>3</b>x</label>
      <RangeField label="Spike length (s)" name="len" min="5" max="30" step="5" value="15" readout="15" />
      <RangeField label="Client timeout (s)" name="to" min="0.5" max="5" step="0.5" value="2" readout="2" />
      <RangeField label="Limit (requests in the system)" name="limit" min="10" max="500" step="10" value="50" readout="50" />
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label class="ls-check"><input type="checkbox" data-deadline /> Server skips requests whose caller has gone</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-run>Run</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-end>Show all</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
      <span class="pg-mono" data-clock></span>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note" data-policynote></p>
    <div class="ls-chart">
      <h3>Requests per second</h3>
      <svg class="ls-svg" viewBox="0 0 600 130" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="Per second: requests offered to the server, answers that arrived within the timeout (goodput), rejected requests, and requests served too late, over 120 seconds with the spike shaded" data-c1>
        <rect data-spike1 y="0" height="130" fill="var(--bad)" opacity=".1" />
        <line data-cap x1="0" x2="600" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="2 3" />
        <path data-offered fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
        <path data-rejected fill="none" stroke="var(--role-4)" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <path data-wasted fill="none" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <path data-goodarea stroke="none" fill="var(--role-3)" opacity=".28" />
        <path data-good fill="none" stroke="var(--role-3)" stroke-width="2.5" />
        <line data-cur1 y1="0" y2="130" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1" opacity=".5" />
      </svg>
      <p class="pg-note"><span class="ls-sw ls-dash"></span>offered (attempts, including retries) <span class="ls-sw" style="background: var(--role-3)"></span>goodput <span class="ls-sw" style="background: var(--role-4)"></span>rejected <span class="ls-sw" style="background: var(--bad)"></span>served too late (wasted). Dotted line: capacity, 100 req/s. Scale capped at <span data-ymax1>400</span>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ls-chart">
      <h3>Latency of answers that arrived in time</h3>
      <svg class="ls-svg" viewBox="0 0 600 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="Average latency in milliseconds of the successful responses each second, against the client timeout, over 120 seconds" data-c2>
        <rect data-spike2 y="0" height="100" fill="var(--bad)" opacity=".1" />
        <line data-to x1="0" x2="600" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="2 3" />
        <path data-lat fill="none" stroke="var(--role-1)" stroke-width="2.5" />
        <line data-cur2 y1="0" y2="100" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1" opacity=".5" />
      </svg>
      <p class="pg-note">Blue: average latency of the useful answers (a gap means none arrived in time). Red dotted line: the client timeout, <span data-toline>2 s</span>. Latency is measured in 100 ms steps.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ls-chart">
      <h3>Requests waiting in the queue</h3>
      <svg class="ls-svg" viewBox="0 0 600 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="Number of requests waiting in the queue at the end of each second, over 120 seconds" data-c3>
        <rect data-spike3 y="0" height="100" fill="var(--bad)" opacity=".1" />
        <path data-q fill="none" stroke="var(--role-2)" stroke-width="2.5" />
        <line data-cur3 y1="0" y2="100" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1" opacity=".5" />
      </svg>
      <p class="pg-note">Queue at the end of each second, peak <span data-qmax>0</span>. Shaded band in every chart: the spike.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-goodbox style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Goodput in the spike</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-good-v>0</span><span class="pg-note" data-good-n></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Latency in the spike</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-lat-v>0</span><span class="pg-note">average of useful answers</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-wastebox style="--c: var(--bad)"><h3>Wasted work</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-waste-v>0</span><span class="pg-note" data-waste-n></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-4)"><h3>Rejected</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-rej-v>0</span><span class="pg-note" data-rej-n></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-5)"><h3>Critical served in the spike</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-crit-v>0</span><span class="pg-note">one request in five is critical</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-recbox style="--c: var(--role-2)"><h3>Recovery after the spike</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-rec-v>0</span><span class="pg-note">until goodput is back to 57+ req/s</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: time moves in 100 ms steps; one request costs 10 ms of work (capacity 100 req/s); 20% of requests are critical; a rejection costs the chosen share of a request and arrives at once. The server cannot see that a client left unless you tick the box (deadline propagation). Adaptive: every second, if any request waited over 300 ms the limit becomes 70% of what is in the system, otherwise it grows by 2 while the system is under pressure. The sizes here are a model, not a benchmark.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue, fmt, prefersReducedMotion, watchVisibility } from '../playground';
  // <core>
  type Policy = 'fifo' | 'bounded' | 'adaptive' | 'lifo' | 'priority';
  type Retry = 'none' | 'naive' | 'backoff';
  interface Params { policy: Policy; mult: number; spikeLen: number; timeoutSec: number; retry: Retry; deadline: boolean; limit: number; rejectPct: number }
  interface Sec { offered: number; good: number; rejected: number; wasted: number; served: number; latSum: number; crit: number; critOffered: number; queue: number }
  interface Attempt { lid: number; cls: number; tries: number; start: number; state: string }
  interface Retried { lid: number; cls: number; tries: number }
  interface Sim { S: Sec[]; rec: number | null; skipped: number }
  const STEP_MS = 100; const PER_SEC = 10; const CAP_MU = 1000; const REQ_MU = 100; const N_SEC = 120; const SPIKE_AT = 10; const BASE = 60; const CAPACITY = 100;
  const AD_TARGET_MS = 300; const AD_START = 100;
  const AD = { min: 5, cut: 0.7, max: 1000, step: 2 }; // adaptive limit: multiply by 0.7 on a latency breach, add 2 under pressure, within 5..1000
  const MAX_TRIES = 3; // first attempt plus two retries
  const BACKOFF = { firstSec: 0.5, jitterMin: 0.5 }; // exponential backoff from 0.5 s, times a jitter of 0.5..1.5
  const JITTER_SLOTS = 1000;
  const EPS = 1e-9; // keeps floor() from losing an arrival to rounding
  const CRITICAL_EVERY = 5; // one request in five is critical
  const RECOVERED = 0.95; // good throughput back at 95% of normal

  function simulate(p: Params): Sim {
    const T = Math.round(p.timeoutSec * PER_SEC); const steps = N_SEC * PER_SEC;
    const spikeStart = SPIKE_AT * PER_SEC; const spikeEnd = (SPIKE_AT + p.spikeLen) * PER_SEC;
    const rejectMu = Math.round((REQ_MU * p.rejectPct) / 100);
    const maxTries = p.retry === 'none' ? 1 : MAX_TRIES;
    const qs = [{ a: [] as Attempt[], h: 0 }, { a: [] as Attempt[], h: 0 }]; // 0 critical, 1 everyone else
    const len = (k: number) => qs[k].a.length - qs[k].h; const total = () => len(0) + len(1);
    const due = new Map<number, Retried[]>(); const dl = new Map<number, Attempt[]>();
    const add = <V,>(m: Map<number, V[]>, k: number, v: V) => { const l = m.get(k); if (l) l.push(v); else m.set(k, [v]); };
    let acc = 0; let nextId = 0; let debt = 0; let adLimit = AD_START; let winBreach = false; let winPressure = false; let skipped = 0;
    const S: Sec[] = Array.from({ length: N_SEC }, () => ({ offered: 0, good: 0, rejected: 0, wasted: 0, served: 0, latSum: 0, crit: 0, critOffered: 0, queue: 0 }));
    const fail = (a: Attempt, i: number, why: string) => { // the client learns at step i that this attempt failed
      a.state = why;
      if (a.tries < maxTries) {
        const jit = (((a.lid * 2654435761) >>> 0) % JITTER_SLOTS) / JITTER_SLOTS; // Knuth multiplicative hash of the request id
        const d = p.retry === 'naive' ? 1 : Math.max(1, Math.round(PER_SEC * BACKOFF.firstSec * 2 ** (a.tries - 1) * (BACKOFF.jitterMin + jit)));
        add(due, i + d, { lid: a.lid, cls: a.cls, tries: a.tries + 1 });
      }
    };
    for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) {
      const s = S[Math.floor(i / PER_SEC)];
      for (const a of dl.get(i) ?? []) if (a.state === 'wait') fail(a, i, 'timeout');
      dl.delete(i);
      const rate = i >= spikeStart && i < spikeEnd ? CAPACITY * p.mult : BASE;
      acc += rate / PER_SEC; const n = Math.floor(acc + EPS); acc -= n;
      const arr: Retried[] = [];
      for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) { const lid = nextId++; arr.push({ lid, cls: lid % CRITICAL_EVERY === 0 ? 0 : 1, tries: 1 }); }
      for (const r of due.get(i) ?? []) arr.push(r);
      due.delete(i);
      let budget = CAP_MU + debt;
      for (const r of arr) {
        const a: Attempt = { lid: r.lid, cls: r.cls, tries: r.tries, start: i, state: 'wait' };
        s.offered++; if (a.cls === 0) s.critOffered++;
        const qlen = total(); let admit = true;
        if (p.policy === 'bounded') admit = qlen < p.limit;
        else if (p.policy === 'adaptive') admit = qlen < adLimit;
        else if (p.policy === 'priority') admit = a.cls === 0 ? qlen < p.limit : qlen < Math.floor(p.limit / 2);
        else if (p.policy === 'lifo' && qlen >= p.limit) { // full: drop the oldest, who is least likely to still be waiting
          const q = qs[1]; const old = q.a[q.h++];
          if (old.state === 'wait') { s.rejected++; budget -= rejectMu; fail(old, i, 'rejected'); }
        }
        if (!admit) { s.rejected++; budget -= rejectMu; fail(a, i, 'rejected'); winPressure = true; }
        else { qs[p.policy === 'priority' ? a.cls : 1].a.push(a); add(dl, i + T, a); }
      }
      while (budget >= REQ_MU) {
        const q = p.policy === 'priority' && len(0) > 0 ? qs[0] : len(1) > 0 ? qs[1] : null;
        if (!q) break;
        const a = (p.policy === 'lifo' ? q.a.pop() : q.a[q.h++]) as Attempt; // LIFO serves the newest
        if (p.deadline && i - a.start >= T) { skipped++; continue; } // caller gone: skip at no cost
        budget -= REQ_MU; s.served++;
        const lat = i - a.start + 1; if ((lat - 1) * STEP_MS > AD_TARGET_MS) winBreach = true;
        if (lat <= T && a.state === 'wait') { a.state = 'ok'; s.good++; s.latSum += lat * STEP_MS; if (a.cls === 0) s.crit++; }
        else s.wasted++; // done for a caller that already timed out
      }
      debt = Math.min(0, budget);
      if (p.policy === 'adaptive' && (i + 1) % PER_SEC === 0) {
        if (winBreach) adLimit = Math.max(AD.min, Math.floor(Math.min(adLimit, total() + 1) * AD.cut));
        else if (winPressure || total() > adLimit / 2) adLimit = Math.min(AD.max, adLimit + AD.step);
        winBreach = false; winPressure = false;
      }
      if ((i + 1) % PER_SEC === 0) s.queue = total();
    }
    let rec: number | null = null; const end = SPIKE_AT + p.spikeLen;
    for (let t = end; t + 2 < N_SEC; t++) if (S[t].good >= BASE * RECOVERED && S[t + 1].good >= BASE * RECOVERED && S[t + 2].good >= BASE * RECOVERED) { /* three good seconds in a row */ rec = t - end; break; }
    return { S, rec, skipped };
  }

  // Totals over the first `upto` seconds; the spike window is clipped to what has been shown.
  function summarise(r: Sim, p: Params, upto: number) {
    const a = SPIKE_AT; const b = Math.min(upto, SPIKE_AT + p.spikeLen); const span = Math.max(0, b - a);
    let good = 0; let lat = 0; let offered = 0; let spikeServed = 0; let spikeRej = 0; let wasted = 0; let rejected = 0; let served = 0; let crit = 0; let critOff = 0; let peakQ = 0;
    for (let t = 0; t < upto; t++) {
      const s = r.S[t]; wasted += s.wasted; rejected += s.rejected; served += s.served; peakQ = Math.max(peakQ, s.queue);
      if (t >= a && t < b) { crit += s.crit; critOff += s.critOffered; good += s.good; lat += s.latSum; offered += s.offered; spikeServed += s.served; spikeRej += s.rejected; }
    }
    const rejectMu = (REQ_MU * p.rejectPct) / 100;
    const busy = span > 0 ? Math.min(1, (spikeServed * REQ_MU + spikeRej * rejectMu) / (span * CAP_MU)) : 0;
    return { span, goodRate: span ? good / span : 0, latMs: good ? lat / good : 0, offeredRate: span ? offered / span : 0, wasted, rejected, served, wastedShare: served ? wasted / served : 0, critShare: critOff ? crit / critOff : 0, peakQ, busy, good };
  }
  // </core>

  const GOOD_BAD = 0.7; // good throughput under 70% of normal is red
  const WASTE_BAD = 100; // wasted requests before the box turns red
  const TICK_MS = 60; // animation step per simulated second
  const NOTES: Record<Policy, string> = {
    fifo: 'Accept everything, serve oldest first. Nothing is refused, so nothing is protected: the queue grows without limit and the oldest requests are the ones whose callers have already left.',
    bounded: 'Reject at once (HTTP 503 or 429) when more than the limit are in the system; accepted requests wait at most limit / capacity. Safe only if that wait is below the client timeout.',
    adaptive: 'The limit starts at 100 and follows queue delay: cut to 70% when requests wait more than 300 ms, otherwise grow slowly (additive increase, multiplicative decrease, like TCP). The slider is not used.',
    lifo: 'Serve the newest request first and, when the limit is reached, drop the oldest. Requests that are about to time out anyway are the ones sacrificed.',
    priority: 'Critical traffic (1 in 5) is served first and admitted up to the limit; everything else is refused once half the limit is in use.',
  };

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ls]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const reduce = prefersReducedMotion();
    const W = 600; let res: Sim; let shown = N_SEC; let timer: number | undefined; let onScreen = true; let raf = 0; let running = false;
    const params = (): Params => ({
      policy: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-policy]').value as Policy, retry: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-retry]').value as Retry,
      rejectPct: Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-reject]').value), mult: val('[data-mult]'), spikeLen: val('[data-len]'),
      timeoutSec: val('[data-to]'), limit: val('[data-limit]'), deadline: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-deadline]').checked,
    });
    function recompute() { res = simulate(params()); schedule(); }
    function schedule() { if (!raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(() => { raf = 0; draw(); }); }
    const X = (t: number) => (((t + 0.5) * W) / N_SEC).toFixed(1);
    // A polyline that breaks where a value is missing (no useful answer that second).
    function path(n: number, f: (t: number) => number | null, y: (v: number) => number) {
      let d = ''; let pen = false;
      for (let t = 0; t < n; t++) { const v = f(t); if (v === null) { pen = false; continue; } d += `${pen ? 'L' : 'M'}${X(t)},${y(v).toFixed(1)}`; pen = true; }
      return d;
    }
    function draw() {
      const p = params(); const S = res.S; const n = Math.max(1, shown);
      q('[data-multval]').textContent = String(p.mult); q('[data-lenval]').textContent = String(p.spikeLen);
      q('[data-toval]').textContent = String(p.timeoutSec); q('[data-limitval]').textContent = String(p.limit);
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-limit]').disabled = p.policy === 'fifo' || p.policy === 'adaptive';
      q('[data-policynote]').textContent = NOTES[p.policy];
      // Charts: scales come from the whole run so the picture does not jump while it plays.
      const C1 = { floor: 128, h: 124, minY: 120, maxY: 400, headroom: 1.05 }, C2 = { floor: 96, h: 92, headroom: 1.1, minQ: 50 }; // SVG plot boxes (match the markup)
      const MS_PER_S = 1000;
      const maxOff = Math.max(...S.map((s) => s.offered)); const ymax1 = Math.max(C1.minY, Math.min(maxOff, C1.maxY)) * C1.headroom;
      const y1 = (v: number) => C1.floor - (Math.min(v, ymax1) / ymax1) * C1.h;
      q('[data-ymax1]').textContent = `${Math.round(ymax1)} req/s`;
      const sx = ((SPIKE_AT * W) / N_SEC); const sw = (p.spikeLen * W) / N_SEC;
      for (const k of ['1', '2', '3']) { const r = q(`[data-spike${k}]`); r.setAttribute('x', sx.toFixed(1)); r.setAttribute('width', sw.toFixed(1)); }
      q('[data-cap]').setAttribute('y1', y1(CAPACITY).toFixed(1)); q('[data-cap]').setAttribute('y2', y1(CAPACITY).toFixed(1));
      q('[data-offered]').setAttribute('d', path(n, (t) => S[t].offered, y1));
      q('[data-rejected]').setAttribute('d', path(n, (t) => S[t].rejected, y1));
      q('[data-wasted]').setAttribute('d', path(n, (t) => S[t].wasted, y1));
      const gd = path(n, (t) => S[t].good, y1);
      q('[data-good]').setAttribute('d', gd);
      q('[data-goodarea]').setAttribute('d', gd ? `${gd}L${X(n - 1)},${C1.floor}L${X(0)},${C1.floor}Z` : '');
      const ymax2 = p.timeoutSec * MS_PER_S * C2.headroom; const y2 = (v: number) => C2.floor - (Math.min(v, ymax2) / ymax2) * C2.h;
      q('[data-to]').setAttribute('y1', y2(p.timeoutSec * MS_PER_S).toFixed(1)); q('[data-to]').setAttribute('y2', y2(p.timeoutSec * MS_PER_S).toFixed(1));
      q('[data-toline]').textContent = `${p.timeoutSec} s`;
      q('[data-lat]').setAttribute('d', path(n, (t) => (S[t].good ? S[t].latSum / S[t].good : null), y2));
      const ymax3 = Math.max(C2.minQ, ...S.map((s) => s.queue)) * C1.headroom; const y3 = (v: number) => C2.floor - (v / ymax3) * C2.h;
      q('[data-q]').setAttribute('d', path(n, (t) => S[t].queue, y3));
      q('[data-qmax]').textContent = fmt(Math.max(0, ...S.slice(0, n).map((s) => s.queue)));
      for (const k of ['1', '2', '3']) { const c = q(`[data-cur${k}]`); c.setAttribute('x1', X(n - 1)); c.setAttribute('x2', X(n - 1)); }
      // Numbers
      const m = summarise(res, p, n); const done = n >= N_SEC;
      q('[data-clock]').textContent = `second ${n} of ${N_SEC}${n > SPIKE_AT && n <= SPIKE_AT + p.spikeLen ? ' (spike)' : ''}`;
      q('[data-good-v]').textContent = m.span ? `${fmt(m.goodRate)} req/s` : 'n/a';
      q('[data-good-n]').textContent = m.span ? `of ${fmt(m.offeredRate)} req/s offered, normal is ${BASE}` : 'spike not reached yet';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-goodbox]').style.setProperty('--c', m.span && m.goodRate < BASE * GOOD_BAD ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-3)');
      q('[data-lat-v]').textContent = m.good ? `${fmt(m.latMs)} ms` : 'none';
      q('[data-waste-v]').textContent = fmt(m.wasted);
      q('[data-waste-n]').textContent = `${Math.round(m.wastedShare * 100)}% of all work done${res.skipped ? `; ${fmt(res.skipped)} stale requests skipped free` : ''}`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-wastebox]').style.setProperty('--c', m.wasted > WASTE_BAD ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--border)');
      q('[data-rej-v]').textContent = fmt(m.rejected);
      q('[data-rej-n]').textContent = m.span ? `server ${Math.round(m.busy * 100)}% busy in the spike, rejections included` : 'before the spike';
      q('[data-crit-v]').textContent = `${Math.round(m.critShare * 100)}%`;
      q('[data-rec-v]').textContent = !done ? '...' : res.rec === null ? 'not recovered' : res.rec === 0 ? 'immediate' : `${res.rec} s`;
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = !m.span ? 'Press Run, or Show all.' : verdict(p, m, done);
      q('[data-run]').textContent = running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
    }
    function verdict(p: Params, m: ReturnType<typeof summarise>, done: boolean) {
      const parts = [`In the spike the server was ${Math.round(m.busy * 100)}% busy, but only ${fmt(m.goodRate)} of ${fmt(m.offeredRate)} requests per second got a useful answer.`];
      if (m.wasted > 100) parts.push(`${Math.round(m.wastedShare * 100)}% of the work it did was for callers that had already given up.`);
      else if (m.rejected > 0) parts.push('Almost no work was wasted on callers that had already given up.');
      if (done) parts.push(res.rec === null ? 'Goodput had not recovered by the end of the 120 s window.' : res.rec === 0 ? 'Goodput was back to normal as soon as the spike ended.' : `Goodput took ${res.rec} s after the spike to return to normal.`);
      return parts.join(' ');
    }
    function stop() { window.clearInterval(timer); timer = undefined; running = false; }
    function advance() { if (shown >= N_SEC) stop(); else shown++; schedule(); }
    function clock() { window.clearInterval(timer); timer = undefined; if (running && onScreen && !document.hidden) timer = window.setInterval(advance, TICK_MS); }
    q('[data-run]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (running) { stop(); schedule(); return; }
      if (shown >= N_SEC) shown = 1;
      if (reduce) { shown = N_SEC; schedule(); return; }
      running = true; clock(); schedule();
    });
    q('[data-end]').addEventListener('click', () => { stop(); shown = N_SEC; schedule(); });
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => { stop(); shown = 1; schedule(); });
    root.querySelectorAll('select, input').forEach((el) => el.addEventListener('input', recompute));
    watchVisibility(root, (on) => { onScreen = on; clock(); });
    recompute();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .ls-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .ls-chart { display: grid; gap: 4px; }
  .playground .ls-svg { width: 100%; display: block; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; height: 120px; }
  .playground .ls-sw { display: inline-block; width: .8em; height: .8em; border-radius: 2px; margin: 0 4px 0 8px; vertical-align: -1px; }
  .playground .ls-sw.ls-dash { background: transparent; border-top: 2px dashed var(--muted); height: 0; margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
